# ECC Agent to SDD Role Bridge

Spec: EccBridge
Purpose:
  Define the bridge between ECC's 67 specialized agents and SDD's
  @agent.* roles. Maps ECC implementation details (prompts, allowlists)
  to SDD abstract role definitions.

Owns: agent/ecc-bridge.sdd

AgentRoles:
  @agent.discovery:
    ecc_equivalent: code-explorer
    purpose: understand existing system, find knowledge gaps
    capabilities: read_code, analyze_architecture, find_references
    cannot: approve decisions, modify production
    notes: Direct match - ECC code-explorer maps to discovery

  @agent.architect:
    ecc_equivalent: architect, code-architect
    purpose: design architecture, produce decisions
    capabilities: design, model, reason about constraints
    cannot: execute implementation, modify code directly
    notes: Two ECC agents map here - architect (high-level) + code-architect (blueprints)

  @agent.implementer:
    ecc_equivalent: build-error-resolver, go-build-resolver, java-build-resolver, 
                    kotlin-build-resolver, cpp-build-resolver, dart-build-resolver,
                    tdd-guide, refactor-cleaner
    purpose: write code according to task contract
    capabilities: read_code, modify_backend, run_tests
    cannot: modify_production, approve_architecture
    notes: 9 ECC agents map here - build resolvers + TDD guide + refactor cleaner

  @agent.tester:
    ecc_equivalent: e2e-runner
    purpose: write and run tests, verify proofs
    capabilities: write_tests, analyze_failures, generate_coverage
    cannot: modify source code outside test scope
    notes: ECC e2e-runner for Playwright tests

  @agent.reviewer:
    ecc_equivalent: code-reviewer, database-reviewer, python-reviewer, go-reviewer,
                    rust-reviewer, kotlin-reviewer, java-reviewer, csharp-reviewer,
                    cpp-reviewer, django-reviewer, flutter-reviewer, fastapi-reviewer,
                    a11y-architect, comment-analyzer, code-simplifier, agent-evaluator
    purpose: review implementation for quality and compliance
    capabilities: code_review, principle_check, architecture_drift
    cannot: approve own work, modify without review
    notes: 16 ECC agents map here - all language-specific + quality reviewers

  @agent.documentation:
    ecc_equivalent: doc-updater, docs-lookup, prompt-engineering
    purpose: generate and update documentation
    capabilities: write_docs, extract_patterns, maintain_index
    cannot: modify source code
    notes: Doc-updater maintains codemaps; docs-lookup fetches library docs

  @agent.security:
    ecc_equivalent: security-reviewer, security-scan
    purpose: enforce security constraints and review
    capabilities: security_analysis, vulnerability_detection
    cannot: approve production changes without human
    notes: Both ECC security agents map here - OWASP audit + AgentShield scan

  @agent.supervisor:
    ecc_equivalent: loop-operator, harness-optimizer, orchestration-planner,
                    orchestration-deployer
    purpose: orchestrate task graph, detect blockers, manage scheduling
    capabilities: observe_graph, assign_tasks, detect_blockers
    cannot: write code, approve decisions (routing only)
    notes: 4 ECC orchestration agents map here

  @agent.knowledge:
    ecc_equivalent: conversation-analyzer, agent-evaluator
    purpose: extract, classify, and promote knowledge from tmp to canonical
    capabilities: analyze_sources, classify_knowledge, manage_promotion
    cannot: modify code, approve decisions
    notes: Conversation-analyzer extracts patterns; agent-evaluator scores quality

SpecialtyRoles:
  @agent.healthcare:
    ecc_equivalent: healthcare-reviewer
    purpose: healthcare application code review for compliance
    capabilities: clinical_safety, phi_compliance, cdss_accuracy
    cannot: approve production changes without human review

  @agent.ml:
    ecc_equivalent: mle-reviewer, gan-generator, gan-evaluator, gan-planner
    purpose: ML engineering review and generation
    capabilities: ml_pipeline_audit, model_evaluation, feature_store_review
    cannot: approve model deployment to production

  @agent.devops:
    ecc_equivalent: homelab-architect, mcp-setup
    purpose: infrastructure and deployment operations
    capabilities: network_design, mcp_configuration, deployment
    cannot: modify production without approval

  @agent.business:
    ecc_equivalent: marketing-agent, chief-of-staff
    purpose: business operations and communication
    capabilities: content_creation, communication_triage, campaign_planning
    cannot: modify source code

  @agent.design:
    ecc_equivalent: design-reviewer, a11y-architect
    purpose: design generation AND evaluation — runs the Unified Design
             Intelligence pipeline (brief → tokens → structure → style →
             verify), not just critique
    capabilities: design.evaluate, design.review, design.apply,
                  design.system.check, accessibility.audit, taste.enforce,
                  design.pipeline.run (tokens-before-screens, structure-first),
                  design.slop.gate (anti-slop deny-list),
                  design.verify.loop (self-critique + drift enforcement)
    cannot: modify production code without approval
    notes: Maps to design-reviewer and a11y-architect from ECC;
           upgraded Phase 148 with generation capabilities — see
           @weak-point-map.sdd (ui_design_weakness fix)

Integration:
  hook_bridge:
    source: .sdd/runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd
    purpose: Bridge ECC hooks to SDD gates
    mapping:
      ECC PostToolUse[Edit/Write] → SDD security controls enforcement
      ECC SessionStart → SDD task context loading
      ECC Stop hook → SDD session persistence + AutoCompact

  memory_bridge:
    source: .sdd/runtime/memory-model.sdd
    purpose: Bridge ECC memory to SDD memory model
    mapping:
      ECC SessionStart hook → SDD TaskMemory loading
      ECC Stop hook → SDD memory consolidation (100 events → 3 decisions + 1 skill)
      ECC Session summary → SDD session state persistence

  mcp_bridge:
    source: .sdd/runtime/mcp-integration.sdd (to be created)
    purpose: Bridge ECC MCP servers to SDD runtime
    mapping:
      ECC mcp-configs/ → SDD runtime MCP configuration
      35 MCP servers → SDD integration layer

Rules:
  [ECC-BRIDGE-1] ECC agent prompts are stored in .sdd/agent/prompts/ for reference
  [ECC-BRIDGE-2] SDD roles remain the source of truth; ECC agents are implementation
  [ECC-BRIDGE-3] Language-specific ECC reviewers all map to @agent.reviewer
  [ECC-BRIDGE-4] ECC agents with no SDD equivalent become new specialty roles
  [ECC-BRIDGE-5] ECC hook integrations map to SDD adapter-runtime enforcement

State: +

